# One assisted selection reaches its original record

Document ID: `reiyah.engine.assisted-inspection-checkpoint`. Version: `0.1.0`.
Date: 14 September 2026. Status: `exploratory`.

A saved selection now traces to the supplied anchor capture. User-supplied screenshots show
the point cloud and save dialog; the user reports clicking a point, seeing it turn white and
pressing Save As. The returned scene contains one selected point, original zero-based index
**28,692**. The existing native adapter verifies all **34,720** original records, including
unselected points, without geometry or attribute changes. A separate reader verifies the raw
record at byte offset **573,840**, corresponding to PLY offset **574,004**.

This is an assisted engineering observation. It supplies no physical object label, unassisted
discovery, reference admission or independently verified operator identity. Both comparison
references remain open; the real detector comparison remains **[-8,8]**.

